# MEMOTE 0.17.0, verified 2026-09-11, digest
# sha256:1009323d7549e7fbb6f30f6ac6380a22967a7c7860acf0044b7346ba78bed098 -- the
# only active tag quay's biocontainers repository serves for this image
# (`curl https://quay.io/api/v1/repository/biocontainers/memote/tag/?onlyActiveTags=true`).
#
# `memote run` and `memote report snapshot` each run the FULL pytest suite
# independently -- `report snapshot` never reads `run`'s own result.json.gz --
# and neither file carries a top-level score: the percentage is assembled by
# `Report.compute_score()`, called only from the report path, which mutates
# the very results object it renders from. `resources/lib/modelling/
# memote_score.py` calls `memote.suite.api.test_model` once and hands that
# SAME object to both `ResultManager.store` (the exact call `memote run`
# makes) and `api.snapshot_report` (which adds the score) -- one test
# execution instead of two, and the score is memote's own number rather than
# something invented here.
#
# This image DOES carry cobra 0.29.0 (MEMOTE needs it to load and test models),
# but neither CarveMe nor reframed nor SMETANA -- confirmed against the actual
# package list, not the metaGEM biocontainer's, which ships none of CarveMe,
# MEMOTE or SMETANA either. `carveme.env` ships reframed, not cobra, for the
# same reason its own comment gives; the two stay separate envs.
#
# Default solver is glpk, open-source and bundled -- no cplex/gurobi problem
# here, unlike `carveme.env`'s.
container: docker://quay.io/biocontainers/memote:0.17.0--pyhdfd78af_0
conda: memote
